.TH CVECTOR_DESTROY 3 "2026-09-28" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cvector_destroy \- destroy a vector and set pointer to NULL
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cvector.h>

cvector_destroy(v)
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Frees everything the vector owns, its data buffer included, and then sets
the vector pointer to NULL.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
v    Vector to destroy. It must be a modifiable lvalue such as a
     variable or an array element; the macro evaluates it exactly once
     and sets it to NULL
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Calling it with a NULL pointer is safe and does nothing.

The elements are not freed one by one, so when they point to heap buffers
the caller has to free those first.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cvector_create (3)
